{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "efb98280",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SEARCH-BP-2.1 minimal-result analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook reads the current `search_bp_results/2` layout directly: one resolved config and one six-field Parquet file per condition. It does not load circuits, samples, corrections, search paths, or truth. Every logical-error denominator is a physical shot; BB's 12 observables are one block trial.\n",
    "\n",
    "Figures compare the three configured decoders within this one run and execution context. Wall latency includes failed decoder calls. Wilson bands describe binomial logical-error uncertainty; Student-t bands describe uncertainty in the arithmetic mean wall latency. They do not establish decoder superiority or production tail behavior."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d8805760",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "get_ipython().run_line_magic(\"matplotlib\", \"inline\")\n",
    "from matplotlib_inline.backend_inline import set_matplotlib_formats\n",
    "set_matplotlib_formats(\"png\")\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from IPython.display import display\n",
    "import analysis\n",
    "from analysis import (\n",
    "    decoder_event_rate_table,\n",
    "    plot_decode_time_histogram,\n",
    "    plot_logical_error_rate,\n",
    "    plot_mean_decode_time,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from analysis import summarize_run\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = next(p for p in (Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents) if (p / \"pyproject.toml\").is_file())\n",
    "RUN_PATH = Path(os.environ.get(\"QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN\", '/home/quantum_teresheys/workspace/beamsearch_decimation/assets/runs/2026_09_22_19_37_199b4d87')).expanduser().resolve()\n",
    "if Path(analysis.__file__).resolve().parent != (ROOT / \"analysis\").resolve():\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(f\"Analysis loaded from another checkout: {analysis.__file__}; Python: {sys.executable}\")\n",
    "if not (RUN_PATH / \"config_resolved.json\").is_file():\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"Not a current simulation run: {RUN_PATH}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "CODES = None\n",
    "PHYSICAL_RATES = None\n",
    "DISTANCES = None\n",
    "DECODERS = None\n",
    "CONFIDENCE = 0.95\n",
    "HISTOGRAM_CODE = \"bb72\"\n",
    "HISTOGRAM_PHYSICAL_RATE = 0.002\n",
    "HISTOGRAM_DISTANCE = 6\n",
    "HISTOGRAM_BINS = 60\n",
    "FIGURE_OUTPUT = ROOT / \"assets\" / \"analysis\" / RUN_PATH.name\n",
    "FIGURE_OUTPUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Run: {RUN_PATH}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Figures: {FIGURE_OUTPUT}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e747313e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Condition-level statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the complete descriptive information supported by the saved schema: block logical errors, all-shot wall latency, and OSD calls over known flags. Failed shots remain in logical-error and latency denominators."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "403cbd71",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summaries = summarize_run(RUN_PATH, confidence=CONFIDENCE)\n",
    "summary_table = pd.DataFrame([{\n",
    "    \"code\": row[\"family\"],\n",
    "    \"distance\": row[\"distance\"],\n",
    "    \"rounds\": row[\"rounds\"],\n",
    "    \"physical_rate\": row[\"physical_rate\"],\n",
    "    \"decoder\": row[\"decoder_name\"],\n",
    "    \"shots\": row[\"shots\"],\n",
    "    \"logical_errors\": row[\"block_failures\"],\n",
    "    \"logical_error_rate\": row[\"logical_error_rate\"][\"rate\"],\n",
    "    \"logical_ci_low\": row[\"logical_error_rate\"][\"low\"],\n",
    "    \"logical_ci_high\": row[\"logical_error_rate\"][\"high\"],\n",
    "    \"mean_wall_ms\": row[\"decode_time\"][\"mean_ns\"] / 1e6,\n",
    "    \"median_wall_ms\": row[\"decode_time\"][\"median_ns\"] / 1e6,\n",
    "    \"p95_wall_ms\": row[\"decode_time\"][\"p95_ns\"] / 1e6,\n",
    "    \"p99_wall_ms\": row[\"decode_time\"][\"p99_ns\"] / 1e6,\n",
    "    \"osd_calls\": row[\"osd_call_fraction\"][\"count\"],\n",
    "    \"osd_known\": row[\"osd_call_fraction\"][\"denominator\"],\n",
    "    \"osd_unknown\": row[\"osd_unknown\"],\n",
    "    \"osd_call_rate\": row[\"osd_call_fraction\"][\"rate\"],\n",
    "} for row in summaries]).sort_values([\"physical_rate\", \"decoder\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "display(summary_table)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76034e3d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Logical error rate\n",
    "\n",
    "Shading is the two-sided 95% Wilson interval. All points have 10,000 physical-shot trials in this run."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a42f36a7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "logical_error_figures = plot_logical_error_rate(\n",
    "    RUN_PATH, codes=CODES, physical_rates=PHYSICAL_RATES, distances=DISTANCES,\n",
    "    decoders=DECODERS, confidence=CONFIDENCE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "for figure in logical_error_figures:\n",
    "    family = figure.axes[0].get_title()\n",
    "    for suffix in (\"png\", \"pdf\"):\n",
    "        figure.savefig(FIGURE_OUTPUT / f\"logical_error_rate_{family}.{suffix}\", dpi=300)\n",
    "    display(figure)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "700f585f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Mean complete-service wall latency\n",
    "\n",
    "Each mean includes every saved shot, including failures. Shading is a 95% Student-t interval for the arithmetic mean. Throughput-mode worker contention is part of these measurements."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0c41cbb2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "decode_time_figures = plot_mean_decode_time(\n",
    "    RUN_PATH, codes=CODES, physical_rates=PHYSICAL_RATES, distances=DISTANCES,\n",
    "    decoders=DECODERS, clock=\"wall\", confidence=CONFIDENCE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "for figure in decode_time_figures:\n",
    "    family = figure.axes[0].get_title()\n",
    "    for suffix in (\"png\", \"pdf\"):\n",
    "        figure.savefig(FIGURE_OUTPUT / f\"mean_wall_latency_{family}.{suffix}\", dpi=300)\n",
    "    display(figure)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "01f2fac0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Wall-latency distribution at p = 0.002\n",
    "\n",
    "Each decoder has its own panel. Vertical lines show the arithmetic mean, p95, and p99. This plot is descriptive; the run does not save CPU time or isolated-latency measurements."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5d3e8f39",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "histogram_figure = plot_decode_time_histogram(\n",
    "    RUN_PATH, code=HISTOGRAM_CODE, physical_rate=HISTOGRAM_PHYSICAL_RATE,\n",
    "    distance=HISTOGRAM_DISTANCE, decoders=DECODERS, clock=\"wall\",\n",
    "    bins=HISTOGRAM_BINS,\n",
    ")\n",
    "for suffix in (\"png\", \"pdf\"):\n",
    "    histogram_figure.savefig(\n",
    "        FIGURE_OUTPUT / f\"wall_latency_histogram_{HISTOGRAM_CODE}_d{HISTOGRAM_DISTANCE}_p002.{suffix}\",\n",
    "        dpi=300,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "display(histogram_figure)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "955d27eb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## OSD call fraction\n",
    "\n",
    "The current schema saves the exact OSD-called flag. The denominator excludes null flags and is shown explicitly in `summary_table`; this run has no unknown flags."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "283d7690",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "decoder_rates = decoder_event_rate_table(\n",
    "    RUN_PATH, codes=CODES, physical_rates=PHYSICAL_RATES,\n",
    "    distances=DISTANCES, decoders=DECODERS,\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(decoder_rates)\n",
    "print(\"Saved figures:\")\n",
    "for path in sorted(FIGURE_OUTPUT.iterdir()):\n",
    "    print(path)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "search-correction-rate",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Correction found directly by search\n",
    "\n",
    "For SEARCH-BP-2.1, `correction_by_search_rate` is the fraction of shots whose local combinatorial search directly constructed a correction satisfying the original H/s. Initial-BP, decimated-BP, OSD, and failed exits are false."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "search-correction-table",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "search_columns = [column for column in decoder_rates.columns\n",
    "                  if column[1] == \"correction_by_search_rate\"]\n",
    "if search_columns:\n",
    "    display(decoder_rates.loc[:, search_columns])\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"correction_by_search is unavailable for this legacy run.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9e863e4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interpretation limits\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyzes one BB72 d6 throughput run with three physical rates. It makes no production, asymptotic, causal, or decoder-advantage claim. The minimal schema cannot recover failure components, logical-observable-specific outcomes, BP iteration counts, search paths, correction weights, CPU time, or internal phase timing."
   ]
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {
  "kernelspec": {
   "display_name": "Python (search_decimation)",
   "language": "python",
   "name": "search_decimation"
  }
 },
